# DTF tier manifest: upgrade (upgrade-with-legacy-data, matrix row 6)
# Profile-set: s3 / single. The #2574/#2584 regression class (legacy ROW-LESS
# Maven objects breaking / leaking across a cloud-storage upgrade) only manifests
# on a real shared object store, so this tier reuses the isolation tier's
# storage.s3 profile and its cross-tenant assertions.
#
# UNLIKE every other tier, `upgrade` drives a TWO-PHASE compose itself (see
# oracle.sh): it stands the stack up on an OLD pre-attribution backend, seeds the
# row-less legacy Maven shape, then swaps ONLY the backend container to the
# candidate image (--backend-image, exported as BACKEND_IMAGE) against the SAME
# postgres+minio volumes and lets migrations run. run.sh still health-gates an
# initial `up` on the candidate; the oracle tears that down (`down -v`) and
# rebuilds from the OLD image, which is a legitimate tier-specific pattern
# explicitly scoped to this tier (run.sh is NOT modified).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the seed + oracle drive many admin/alice logins and
# Maven PUTs back-to-back through a single admin; the base default (ON) would
# throttle them. Matches the isolation tier / proof rig. (Base default stays ON;
# a tier disabling a shipped control does so explicitly, per design 2.2.)
#
# UPGRADE_ORIGINS (#2688): the ordered set of "legacy deployment" backends the
# stack is stood up on in PHASE 1, one full in-place swap per origin. Each entry
# is "image|label|note". An origin must be a migration ANCESTOR the candidate can
# reconcile in PHASE 2 (either an exact-checksum prefix, OR a diverged release
# history the candidate's repair_release_1_5_x_divergence step reconciles) so the
# in-place volume upgrade runs the candidate's NEW migrations instead of erroring.
#
#   * v1.5.6-origin — released 1.5.6 (max migration slot 153, NO divergence, NO
#     maven_flat_object_owner attribution table). The candidate's repair step
#     NO-OPS and the migrator applies 154..HEAD fresh: the "no-op / no-divergence"
#     case (issue #2688). A clean boot proves the repair correctly does nothing.
#   * v1.5.7-origin — nexus2457-v157base (release/1.5.x, migrations 151-154, NO
#     attribution table): the historical default and load-bearing #2574/#2584
#     row-less-Maven payload.
#   * v1.5.8-origin — released 1.5.8 (slots 154 AND 155 diverged: the attribution
#     table shipped as 155 on release/1.5.x and was renumbered to 163 on main).
#     The candidate must reconcile the 155->163 renumber and apply 168 fresh.
#
# base-2504 (the isolation coder's pre-#2504 image) still CANNOT be an OLD image
# here — it is not a clean-reconcilable ancestor. See MATRIX-ROW.md.
#
# The v1.5.6/v1.5.8 images are the real published release images the release-gate
# S3 runners already have access to (ghcr.io/artifact-keeper/artifact-keeper-
# backend:<ver>). UPGRADE_OLD_IMAGE stays defined for backward-compat: overriding
# it alone (with no UPGRADE_ORIGINS) drives the single-origin legacy behavior.
# UPGRADE_ONLY="v1.5.6-origin v1.5.8-origin" narrows a local run by label.
PROFILES="storage.s3"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPGRADE_OLD_IMAGE="${UPGRADE_OLD_IMAGE:-ak-backend:nexus2457-v157base}"
UPGRADE_ORIGINS=(
  "ghcr.io/artifact-keeper/artifact-keeper-backend:1.5.6|v1.5.6-origin|max slot 153, no divergence; repair no-ops, migrator applies 154..HEAD fresh"
  "${UPGRADE_OLD_IMAGE}|v1.5.7-origin|slot 154, pre-attribution base; #2574/#2584 row-less-Maven payload"
  "ghcr.io/artifact-keeper/artifact-keeper-backend:1.5.8|v1.5.8-origin|slots 154+155 diverged; candidate reconciles 155->163 renumber + applies 168 fresh"
)
